hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18249","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun, Said informed us from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Mina while upon his mount which was chewing its cud with its saliva flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Allah Almighty has apportioned for every person his share of inheritance, so no bequest is allowed for an heir. The child belongs to the bed and the adulterer gets the stone. Verily whoever claims another father or allies himself to other than his patrons out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people. Ibn Jafar said: And Said said: Matar said: Nothing is accepted from him, neither optional nor obligatory. Yazid said: And in his hadith: Nothing is accepted from him, neither optional nor obligatory, or obligatory nor optional. My father said: Yazid said in his hadith: Amr ibn Kharijah narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them upon his mount."
"18250","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: I was holding the bridle of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while it was chewing its cud with its saliva flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Allah Almighty has given every holder of right his right, and there is no bequest for an heir. The child belongs to the bed and the adulterer gets the stone, and whoever claims another father or attaches himself to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people. Affan said: And Hammam added in it with this chain and did not mention Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm: And I was beneath the throat of his mount. And he added in it: Neither obligatory nor optional is accepted from him. And in the hadith of Hammam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed and said out of aversion to them."
"18251","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed while upon his she-camel and I was beneath its throat while it was chewing its cud with its saliva flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Allah Almighty has given every holder of right his right, and there is no bequest for an heir. The child belongs to the bed and the adulterer gets the stone, and whoever claims another father or attaches himself to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people. Neither optional nor obligatory is accepted from him."
"18252","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Layth from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Amr ibn Kharijah al-Thumali, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the sacrificial animal that gets injured. He said: Slaughter it and dye its sandal in its blood and strike it upon its side, or he said upon its flank, and neither you nor your traveling companions shall eat anything of it."
"18253","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Layth from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Amr al-Thumali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent sacrificial animals with my father. He said: When any of them gets injured, slaughter it then strike its hoof in its blood then strike its side with it, and neither you nor your traveling companions shall eat, and leave it between it and the people."
"18254","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Said that is Ibn Abi Arubah informed us from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm that Amr ibn Kharijah al-Khushani narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them upon his mount while his mount was chewing its cud and its saliva flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Allah Almighty has apportioned for every person his share of inheritance, so no bequest for an heir is allowed. The child belongs to the bed and the adulterer gets the stone. Verily whoever claims another father or allies himself to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people. Allah accepts from him neither optional nor obligatory, or obligatory nor optional."
"18255","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Said informed us from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us while at Mina upon his mount, and I was beneath the throat of his she-camel while it was chewing its cud with its saliva flowing between my shoulders, and he said: Allah Almighty has apportioned for every person his share of inheritance, and no bequest for an heir is allowed. Verily the child belongs to the bed and the adulterer gets the stone. Verily whoever claims another father or allies himself to other than his patrons out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people."
"18256","Said said: And Matar narrated to us from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Amr ibn Kharijah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, and Matar added in the hadith: And neither optional nor obligatory is accepted from him."
"18257","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us and mentioned the hadith, and he said: Matar said: And neither optional nor obligatory is accepted from him, or obligatory nor optional. This is the end of the Musnad of the Syrians."
